==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-fielder.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːldə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|feldere|t=one who works in the field; rustic}}, from {{inh|en|ang|feldeware|t=field-dweller}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|field|er|id2=inhabitant}}. The baseball sense is from 1832.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[dog]] trained in pursuit of game in the field.
# {{lb|en|baseball|softball}} A [[defensive]] player in the [[field]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[fieldworker]].

